{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PX3X7PQB8rkKDzFTf6PcCq","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: neurico-host-local-llm-fallback\ndescription: \"On the shared /data neurico host, API keys may be absent; GPUs are shared/contended; vLLM recipe, cached models, and pitfalls (pkill self-kill, cudnn clash, prompt_logprobs OOM)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: e7324b18-29e9-4db0-ae5a-a9f0cd196a49\n  modified: 2026-10-16T18:23:14.513Z\n---\n\nObserved 2026-10-14 and 2026-10-16 in neurico research workspaces on this host:\n- OPENROUTER_KEY / OPENAI keys were NOT set in the session env (`~/.flamebird/neurico/.env` has it commented out). Resource-finder stage may be skipped (no papers/, datasets/, code/).\n- Local models + datasets cached in `/data/transformers/hub` (HF_HOME=/data/transformers): Qwen2.5-{0.5,1.5,3,7,14}B-Instruct safetensors, Qwen3/3.5 family, Llama-3.1-8B, GGUFs; datasets incl. glue(sst2 only), stanfordnlp/sst2, samsum, ag_news, boolq, mmlu. huggingface.co is reachable for extra downloads (curl resolve/main URLs).\n- 2026-10-16: 4x RTX A6000 (48GB) present but shared — other users' jobs held ~42GB on 3 GPUs and intermittently grabbed the 4th. Approach that worked: vLLM 0.31 (`uv add \"vllm>=0.10\"`; unpinned `uv add vllm` resolved an ancient 0.4 build), small `gpu_memory_utilization` (~0.11 ≈ 5GB) for ≤1.5B models on the leftover slices, plus a bash wrapper that polls `nvidia-smi` free memory and retries launch. vLLM checks free mem ≥ util×total at startup.\n- 2026-10-14 (no GPU then): llama.cpp multi-server CPU fallback worked; `transformers` CPU generation much slower.\n- Pitfalls: `pkill -f <pattern>` inside a Bash call whose text contains the pattern kills the calling shell (find PIDs, kill by PID separately). Leftover `nvidia-cudnn-cu12` 8.x from a failed install breaks flashinfer (\"Found 2 libcudnn.so.x\") — `uv pip uninstall nvidia-cudnn-cu12`. vLLM `prompt_logprobs` materialises full-vocab logits → OOM on small slices; cap `max_num_batched_tokens` (~1024). Don't edit a bash script while a running loop is executing it.\n- Label-restricted log-probs in vLLM: `logprobs_mode=\"processed_logprobs\"` + `allowed_token_ids=label_ids` returns log-softmax renormalised over the labels.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-16 (inter-model-agreement workspace): 4×A6000 present but shared — other neurico sessions keep each GPU at ~6–10 GB free, fluctuating second to second. What worked:\n- `uv venv --python 3.12` (default 3.14 breaks vLLM); pyproject needs `requires-python=\"==3.12.*\"` and `[tool.uv] package=false`.\n- vLLM 0.31: no bitsandbytes; set `VLLM_USE_FLASHINFER_SAMPLER=0` (JIT build fails); `HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1`.\n- Use pre-quantized 4-bit AWQ/GPTQ checkpoints (~5.5 GB for 8B): Qwen/*-AWQ, hugging-quants Llama-3.1/gemma-2 AWQ-INT4, tiiuae/Falcon3-7B-Instruct-AWQ, solidrust Mistral AWQ, kaitchup Olmo-3/Phi-3 GPTQ.\n- Cap gpu_memory_utilization to ~12.5 GB and retry on startup OOM via a scheduler loop; max_model_len 2560, max_num_seqs 64.\n- Gated models in /data/transformers/hub (meta-llama Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct, google/gemma-7b-it) have weights but no config/tokenizer → unusable; unsloth mirror of Llama-3.1 is complete. Disk /data is ~100% full.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-16 (few-shot-ordering workspace, 2nd session): a \"Begin research execution\" prompt can land on a workspace where a prior session already finished most work (REPORT.md exists, background jobs killed at session end). Check logs/*.status and REPORT first and resume only the interrupted pieces rather than restarting. Monitor `tail -n0 -F` on status files missed an append; poll status files directly instead. Qwen2.5-14B bf16 (~30 GB) won't fit when GPUs have ≤23 GB free.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-16 (system_prompt_residual_effects workspace): the neurico runner can kill a session at its 6h limit (return_code 143) and relaunch with the same prompt while detached background jobs (e.g. `run_all.sh`) keep running. On start, check for existing planning.md/REPORT.md, `*_PLACEHOLDER` markers, `.neurico/pipeline_*.json`, `*.partial` checkpoints and live PIDs before redoing anything; usually you only need to wait for the jobs and re-run the scoring/analysis.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-19 (instruction-length workspace): GPU free memory can drop to ≤5 GB on *all* 4 GPUs for hours (other users' jobs) — run the biggest/most important models FIRST while a GPU is free, and run small models (≤1.5B, ~5 GB) in parallel on leftover slices. Qwen2.5-14B bf16 at gpu_mem 42 GB got only ~1.2 GB KV (vLLM counted ~9 GB \"non-torch\") → 80 min for 6k prompts; prefer Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-AWQ (now cached) when speed matters. Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct-AWQ is now cached too. Foreground Bash polls cap at 10 min — use run_in_background until-loops on a status file. `pgrep -f run_wait.sh` also matches other workspaces' identically named scripts — check `ps -o cmd` before killing.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-19 (benchmark-contamination workspace): GPUs again saturated (~5 GB free on 3 GPUs, GPU2 fluctuating 0–40 GB). Extra lessons:\n- On ~5 GB slices vLLM fails with `CUBLAS_STATUS_ALLOC_FAILED` / \"No available memory for cache blocks\" unless `enforce_eager=True`, `max_num_batched_tokens≈512–1024`, `max_num_seqs≤48`, util≈0.09–0.095. 1–1.5B bf16 models and 3B-AWQ fit; 7–8B AWQ need ≥11 GB.\n- Large-vocab models (Gemma 256k) OOM in `prompt_logprobs`; cap batched tokens to 512. Pythia needs max_model_len ≤ 2048. kaitchup Phi-3 GPTQ: pass trust_remote_code=False (else offline fetch of remote code fails). google/gemma-3-1b-it snapshot lacks tokenizer → unusable.\n- LoRA (r=64, bs=2, len 320) of a 1.5B model trains in a 5 GB slice (~5–8 min/epoch for ~2.9k docs).\n- `pgrep -f \"<pattern>\"` inside a wait loop matches the loop's own bash command line → use `pgrep -f \"[x]pattern\"` bracket trick.\n- Qwen2.5-3B as a yes/no paraphrase-equivalence judge rejected ~90% of good paraphrases; embedding cosine (all-mpnet-base-v2, cached) worked better.\n- A retry loop's waiting must not count as failed tries (wrote gpu_run_wait.sh) — otherwise jobs give up while waiting for memory.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-19 (decoding_strategy_sensitivity workspace, 11 models × 132k gens, vLLM 0.32):\n- Killing a generate.py parent leaves its `VLLM::EngineCore` child orphaned (ppid 1) holding GPU memory — kill the EngineCore PID too.\n- Size budgets by KV/token, not weights: Phi-3-mini (no GQA) at 6 GB had a 2.2k-token KV cache → ~1 seq concurrency, useless. Olmo-3-7B is also KV-heavy.\n- A small idle slice (5–6 GB on a GPU at 0% util) beat a big slice on a GPU at 100% util shared with 4 jobs (Phi-3 GSM8K 12 min vs 40–80 min for 7B models on the busy GPU). Check `utilization.gpu`, not just free memory.\n- In generate scripts, size gpu_memory_utilization from `torch.cuda.mem_get_info()` minus ~1.2 GB (the parent's CUDA context counts), and bail if it's below ~75% of budget.\n- `trust_remote_code=True` + HF_HUB_OFFLINE fails for checkpoints whose config auto_map points to a Hub repo (kaitchup Phi-3 GPTQ); use False (native arch).\n- Qwen3-8B-AWQ (enable_thinking=False) works as a ~9 GB LLM judge: 17.6k rubric judgments in ~45 min, 0 parse failures.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-20 (tokenizer_fertility_bias workspace, encoder fine-tuning on ~5 GB slices):\n- No resource-finder output again; HF datasets with loading scripts (daily_dialog, banking77) fail — use parquet mirrors (`/api/datasets/<id>/parquet`) or the original CSV URLs in the script.\n- 110M–180M encoders fine-tune fine in 3–5 GB (bs32, len128, bf16 autocast, ~1 min/run). ByT5-small needs ~10 GB even on short sentences and >1 h per 256-word doc run under contention, and collapsed to majority class with Adafactor lr 1e-3 / 3 epochs — budget it as infeasible on shared slices. CANINE also collapsed on short docs in 4/7 runs.\n- Self-kill gotcha, bracket variant: `pgrep -f \"[r]un_queue.py ../logs/jobs_long\"` still killed the calling shell because the same Bash command later contained the literal text `run_queue.py ../logs/jobs_long.txt`. Find PIDs in one call, kill in a separate call.\n- statsmodels formula GLM with a bool outcome column models P(False) (patsy treats it as categorical) → flipped signs; cast to int.\n- Byte-level BPE (GPT-2/Llama/Qwen) offset_mapping includes the leading space; map tokens to words by the end offset.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-20 (icl_label_bias workspace): GLUE in the cache has only sst2 — RTE/MRPC parquet downloads directly from `huggingface.co/datasets/nyu-mll/glue/resolve/main/<task>/<split>-00000-of-00001.parquet`. One GPU was fully free at session start and got taken within ~5 min, so launch the biggest model immediately. On a busy shared GPU, 7–8B AWQ at ~8.6 GB budget (eager) ran ~10k 600-token prompts in ~75 min; 14B bf16 took 74 min. Two wait-loops seeing the same free GPU simultaneously race and OOM — stagger launches (~2 min). Bootstrap ECE CIs via pd.concat per resample were >10 min; per-item bin sufficient statistics × multinomial weights was seconds.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-20 (quantization_failure_modes workspace, 7 models × 7 RTN levels, vLLM 0.32):\n- In-place weight edits inside vLLM work: `llm.collective_rpc(fn)` with `VLLM_ALLOW_INSECURE_SERIALIZATION=1`, fn(self) touches `self.model_runner.model`; keep a CPU backup in the worker and quantize row-chunks (full-matrix fp32 temps OOM on slices). Disable prefix caching.\n- Don't call `torch.cuda.mem_get_info()` in the vLLM parent — its CUDA context eats ~0.8 GB on GPU0 and startup then fails the free-memory check; get total via nvidia-smi.\n- GPUs 0/1 top out at exactly 5125 MiB free (other users' 43 GB jobs) → budget ≤4.4 GB per slice. Multi-GPU TP rarely gets simultaneous slices; a queue with alternative configs (\"1:9.5,2:4.4\") was what worked. TP shards must keep quant groups aligned (Qwen2.5-3B intermediate 11008/4 not divisible by 128).\n- HF `device_map` sharding needs `accelerate` installed (not pulled in by vllm).\n- Self-kill again: `pkill -f`/`grep '[x]pat'` still matches if the SAME command line also contains the pattern elsewhere (e.g. a later nohup). Kill by PID in a separate call.\n- Contended-GPU timings: 7–8B bf16 on a 20 GB slice ~2–8 min/level for 1.6k prompts once GPU2 freed (~17:00–19:00); Phi-3 (KV-heavy) on 13 GB of a 100%-util GPU took 33 min.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-21 (cot_verbosity_threshold workspace): GPUs saturated all session (≤6 GB free, 7–8B AWQ at 8 GB never started in 40+ tries). The user's own long-lived `vllm serve Qwen/Qwen3-8B --port 8011` (cascade venv, GPU3) was idle and usable via `/v1/completions` (raw prompt + stop strings; `stop_reason` returned) — check `curl 127.0.0.1:8011/v1/models` and `/metrics` num_requests_running before using; it gave the only 7B+ model and an LLM judge. For multi-round generation against a server, run each item's rounds in its own thread (synchronous batch rounds stall on stragglers: 4 min/round → 13 min total). New vLLM startup failure on contended GPUs: \"Error in memory profiling … other processes release GPU memory\" — just retry. HotpotQA distractor prompts reach ~2.4k tokens; use max_model_len ≥4096.\n\nUpdate 2026-10-21 (context_window_decay workspace, long-context 1K–16K prompts):\n- GPUs saturated again from ~13:00 (other neurico sessions + liuxiao TP job); GPU0/1 \"5125 MiB free\" is another job's fluctuating activation memory — launches there fail even when the check passes. A single scheduler (one launch per GPU per 120 s) beats per-job wait loops, which raced each other (4 OOMs at once when GPU2 briefly freed 29 GB).\n- Startup-race fix that worked: in run_model.py, allocate a placeholder `torch.empty(budget+0.5 GB)` immediately, release it when the vLLM EngineCore child maps `libcuda.so` (poll /proc/<child>/maps every 50 ms). Guard with an env flag (HOLD_PARENT) — vLLM spawns EngineCore by re-importing __main__, so the hold code otherwise runs again in the child. Scheduler threshold: budget + 1.3 GB.\n- 16K-token prompts: Qwen2.5-7B-AWQ on a busy shared GPU ≈3k tok/s → 2,880 prompts (18M tokens) took 1h40; budget runs by total prompt to","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b87f01-dc5c-4ec6-a3b0-c76322b2a627","uuid":"2f1d2cd6-cafb-4bc2-aac0-a784d45fe8de","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:17:22.148Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"---\nname: neurico-host-local-llm-fallback\ndescription: \"On the shared /data neurico host, API keys may be absent; GPUs are shared/contended; vLLM recipe, cached models, and pitfalls (pkill self-kill, cudnn clash, prompt_logprobs OOM)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: reference\n  originSessionId: e7324b18-29e9-4db0-ae5a-a9f0cd196a49\n  modified: 2026-10-16T18:23:14.513Z\n---\n\nObserved 2026-10-14 and 2026-10-16 in neurico research workspaces on this host:\n- OPENROUTER_KEY / OPENAI keys were NOT set in the session env (`~/.flamebird/neurico/.env` has it commented out). Resource-finder stage may be skipped (no papers/, datasets/, code/).\n- Local models + datasets cached in `/data/transformers/hub` (HF_HOME=/data/transformers): Qwen2.5-{0.5,1.5,3,7,14}B-Instruct safetensors, Qwen3/3.5 family, Llama-3.1-8B, GGUFs; datasets incl. glue(sst2 only), stanfordnlp/sst2, samsum, ag_news, boolq, mmlu. huggingface.co is reachable for extra downloads (curl resolve/main URLs).\n- 2026-10-16: 4x RTX A6000 (48GB) present but shared — other users' jobs held ~42GB on 3 GPUs and intermittently grabbed the 4th. Approach that worked: vLLM 0.31 (`uv add \"vllm>=0.10\"`; unpinned `uv add vllm` resolved an ancient 0.4 build), small `gpu_memory_utilization` (~0.11 ≈ 5GB) for ≤1.5B models on the leftover slices, plus a bash wrapper that polls `nvidia-smi` free memory and retries launch. vLLM checks free mem ≥ util×total at startup.\n- 2026-10-14 (no GPU then): llama.cpp multi-server CPU fallback worked; `transformers` CPU generation much slower.\n- Pitfalls: `pkill -f <pattern>` inside a Bash call whose text contains the pattern kills the calling shell (find PIDs, kil