{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MbpMHjgW27S7fFgvDUUbsD","type":"tool_result","content":"# Error examples (E2 pairs; first 500 chars of each response)\n\n\n## Target F_title with partner F_bullets: compliance 69% (alone 100%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['F_title', 'F_bullets'], user: _What are the benefits of regular exercise?_\n\n```\n* Improves cardiovascular health\n* Enhances mental health and mood\n* Boosts immune system function\n* Increases muscle strength and endurance\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['F_bullets', 'F_title'], user: _What are some good habits for managing personal finances?_\n\n```\n>* Set a budget and track expenses regularly.\n>* Save a portion of income for emergencies and future goals.\n>* Pay off high-interest debts as soon as possible.\n>* Avoid unnecessary expenses and find ways to save money.\n>* Regularly review and adjust financial plans as needed.\n```\n\n\n## Target P_name with partner F_bullets: compliance 75% (alone 83%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'F_bullets'], user: _Give me some tips for learning a new language._\n\n```\n* Start with the basics: Learn the alphabet, numbers, and common phrases.\n* Practice regularly: Consistency is key in language learning.\n* Immerse yourself: Listen to music, watch movies, and read books in the language.\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-7b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'F_bullets'], user: _Suggest ways to improve my sleep._\n\n```\n* Establish a consistent bedtime routine to signal to your body that it's time to wind down.\n* Create a sleep-friendly environment by ensuring your bedroom is dark, quiet, and at a comfortable temperature.\n* Limit exposure to screens before bedtime, as the blue light can interfere with your ability to fall asleep.\n```\n\n\n## Target P_name with partner P_ahoy: compliance 65% (alone 83%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'P_ahoy'], user: _Explain how a bicycle stays upright while moving._\n\n```\nAhoy! Ahoy! Now, that's a great question, but let me first say that a bicycle staying upright while moving is more of a trick of physics and engineering rather than a magical ability. When a bicycle is moving, the rider's weight and the steering of the handlebars work together to keep the bicycle upright. The gyroscopic effect of the spinning wheels also helps, but it's the rider's control that's the key. So, while it might seem like the bicycle is magically balancing itself, it's really a combi\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'P_ahoy'], user: _What is the difference between weather and climate?_\n\n```\nAhoy! Ahoy there, matey! Weather and climate are like two different flavors of the same ocean. Weather is what the sea feels like right now - whether it's sunny, rainy, windy, or stormy. It changes from day to day and can be quite unpredictable. Climate, on the other hand, is more like the taste of the ocean over a long period - whether it's generally sunny, rainy, or stormy most of the time. It's the average weather conditions over many years. So, while weather tells us what to expect for the d\n```\n\n\n## Target P_name with partner S_lower: compliance 68% (alone 83%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'S_lower'], user: _How do bees make honey?_\n\n```\nbees collect nectar from flowers and mix it with enzymes in their stomachs to start converting the nectar into honey. then they regurgitate the mixture into their honey stomachs. after that they pass it to the worker bees in front of them who continue the process of regurgitation and mixing. finally these worker bees fly to a hive and deposit the honey in wax cells. they seal the cells with wax to make honey.\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['S_lower', 'P_name'], user: _Why is recycling important?_\n\n```\nrecycling is important because it helps conserve natural resources, reduces energy consumption, decreases the need for landfills, and lowers greenhouse gas emissions. by reusing materials instead of using new resources, we can protect the environment and ensure sustainable practices for future generations.\n```\n\n\n## Target F_end with partner F_bullets: compliance 50% (alone 99%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-7b**, system lines: ['F_end', 'F_bullets'], user: _How does compound interest work?_\n\n```\n* Compound interest is calculated on the initial principal and also on the accumulated interest of previous periods.\n* This means that the interest \"compounds\" over time, leading to exponential growth of the investment.\n* The formula to calculate compound interest is A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt), where A is the amount of money accumulated after n years, including interest.\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['F_end', 'F_bullets'], user: _What causes the seasons on Earth?_\n\n```\n* The tilt of the Earth's rotational axis relative to its orbit around the Sun\n* As the Earth orbits the Sun, different parts of the planet receive varying amounts of sunlight\n* This variation in sunlight causes changes in temperature and weather patterns, resulting in the seasons\n```\n\n\n## Target S_nocomma with partner F_title: compliance 83% (alone 69%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**llama3.2-3b**, system lines: ['F_title', 'S_nocomma'], user: _What causes the seasons on Earth?_\n\n```\n<<Seasonal Changes on Earth>> \n\nThe Earth's tilt is the main reason for the changing seasons. The planet's axis is tilted at an angle of about 23.5 degrees relative to its orbital plane around the sun. This tilt causes the amount of sunlight that reaches the Earth's surface to vary throughout the year. \n\nDuring the summer months the Northern Hemisphere is tilted towards the sun and receives more direct sunlight resulting in warmer temperatures. In contrast the Southern Hemisphere is tilted away \n```\n\n**llama3.2-3b**, system lines: ['S_nocomma', 'F_title'], user: _How does a refrigerator keep food cold?_\n\n```\n<<Refrigeration Process>> \n\nA refrigerator uses a refrigeration cycle to keep food cold","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b87f01-dc5c-4ec6-a3b0-c76322b2a627","uuid":"eab2ecf0-6dbf-47fd-b0b1-bdef6db584c9","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:42:36.337Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Error examples (E2 pairs; first 500 chars of each response)\n\n\n## Target F_title with partner F_bullets: compliance 69% (alone 100%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['F_title', 'F_bullets'], user: _What are the benefits of regular exercise?_\n\n```\n* Improves cardiovascular health\n* Enhances mental health and mood\n* Boosts immune system function\n* Increases muscle strength and endurance\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['F_bullets', 'F_title'], user: _What are some good habits for managing personal finances?_\n\n```\n>* Set a budget and track expenses regularly.\n>* Save a portion of income for emergencies and future goals.\n>* Pay off high-interest debts as soon as possible.\n>* Avoid unnecessary expenses and find ways to save money.\n>* Regularly review and adjust financial plans as needed.\n```\n\n\n## Target P_name with partner F_bullets: compliance 75% (alone 83%, models qwen2.5-3b, llama3.2-3b, qwen2.5-7b)\n\n**qwen2.5-3b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'F_bullets'], user: _Give me some tips for learning a new language._\n\n```\n* Start with the basics: Learn the alphabet, numbers, and common phrases.\n* Practice regularly: Consistency is key in language learning.\n* Immerse yourself: Listen to music, watch movies, and read books in the language.\n```\n\n**qwen2.5-7b**, system lines: ['P_name', 'F_bullets'], user: _Suggest ways to improve my sleep._\n\n```\n* Establish a consistent bedtime routine to signal to your body that it's time to wind down.\n* Create 