{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYy9QGve3Ta5gihjeZyJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The study is finished: all 8 models ran on the full design, and `REPORT.md` and `README.md` contain the actual results. Instruction count is the main driver of non-compliance. The ordering, repetition and category effects you predicted point the right way but are much smaller than hypothesized.\n\n**Setup.** There were no API keys on this host, so everything used real open-weight models run locally with greedy decoding:\n- **Models:** 8 models from 0.5B to 8B (Qwen2.5 0.5/1.5/3/7B, Llama-3.2 1/3B, Llama-3.1-8B, Qwen3-8B).\n- **Prompts:** each model got the same 5,120 system-prompt configurations, built from 10 instructions that can all be met together, paired with 40 neutral user requests I wrote.\n- **Scoring:** every response was checked with deterministic code; I hand-checked samples of the failures and they were genuine.\n- **Extra check:** I re-ran part of the design with the instructions as a numbered list on 4 models, and the patterns held.\n\n| Hypothesis | Result |\n|---|---|\n| H1: over 90% with one instruction → 50–65% with 5 or more | **Partly true.** Only 4 of 8 models clear 90% with a single instruction; Qwen2.5-0.5B and 1.5B manage 43% and 60%. Averaged across models, per-instruction compliance goes 83% (1) → 70% (5) → 59% (10). The share of responses meeting *all* instructions falls much faster: 37% at 5 and 5% at 10. Even Qwen3-8B meets all 10 only 24% of the time. |\n| H2: format/length cuts persona/style by 20–30 points | **Mostly not.** The extra drop is 5–12 points in 4 of 8 models, and 20–30 points only in the two smallest. The real pattern is specific to certain instructions: \"exactly 3 bullets\" makes models output only bullets and drop the closing phrase (−30 points), required keywords (−20) and the self-introduction. Some pairs help each other: the no-comma rule is followed more often next to structural instructions. |\n| H3: last position beats first by 15–25 points | **Not supported in size.** Overall it is +1.7 points. Qwen models gain 5–8 points from being last; Llama models gain nothing. |\n| H4: repeating an instruction gives +10–15 points, costs others 5–8 | **Not supported in size.** Repetition gives +3.3 points. Other instructions lose 0.9 points, but adding a neutral filler line costs exactly the same, so that loss comes from the longer prompt, not from repetition. |\n| H5: smaller models decay faster | **Depends on how you measure it.** Relative to their own one-instruction score, smaller models lose a much larger share (strong correlation with size, ρ = −0.95). In absolute percentage points there is no size trend. On an odds scale, which corrects for models starting near 0% or 100%, the 8B models actually decay at least as steeply. |\n\n**One problem during the runs.** While taking an interim snapshot I moved the Qwen2.5-7B output file as it was still being written, and 3,120 of its 5,120 generations were lost. I re-generated them later with the same prompts and settings but different batching, so the 7B model is complete. This is noted in the report's limitations.\n\n**Other limits.** The largest models are 8B, and most local models are 4-bit quantized. \"Persona\" and \"style\" are tested through word-level markers (\"Ahoy\", \"Captain Byte\"), not overall tone. No papers had been pre-gathered for this workspace, so the literature context comes from background knowledge.\n\nAll my GPU workers are stopped. I also added this session's lessons for this shared machine to my memory notes. Everything is in the project folder; start with `REPORT.md`, which links to the figures, result tables and raw generations."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":200597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1160},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b87f01-dc5c-4ec6-a3b0-c76322b2a627","uuid":"f3069d06-3f42-4b2d-adf2-c696641f9870","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:24:46.263Z","request_id":"req_011CgYy9Q6G8XVbWpNsFbEzy"}
